  "overview": "**Vant** is a light-first design system anchored on `#fff` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (19.7:1 contrast) and `#ff976a` brand accent.\n\nTypography centers cleanly on `System UI` (160px display down to 16px body), unified by `4px` base corner radius and subtle shadow elevation.\n\nMaintained by **Youzan**. Source: published token package, package `vant`. Inventory: **28** colors, **14** typography steps, and **38** documented components (MIT license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 38 component tokens with documented paddings: `0 4px`, `8px 16px`, `0 3px`, `16px`, `0 16px`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `#f7f8fa` cards; separate sibling sections using `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Layered Shadow Model**: Uses documented shadows (`0 3px 1px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, .05)`) paired with `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` borders for elevated overlays.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `#ff976a` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `#fff` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `#0b0b0c` secondary labels.\n- Use `#ff976a` with `#0b0b0c` text (9.3:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `System UI` headings with `System UI` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `4px` base geometry across inputs and buttons (4px on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `#f7f8fa` surface shifts and `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `4px` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `van-password-input` fields and secondary buttons."
